@andyzhangx it would be great if Azure cloud provider did not provide any labels when it's actually not configured (i.e. the external one is used). Is there an easy way to detect that in the admission plugin in the API server?

`GetCloudProvider` [here](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/d9d45306df052aa5824fd8b2dab4e61f5ecc481c/plugin/pkg/admission/storage/persistentvolume/label/admission.go#L285-L285) _could_ return some error + the admission _would_ ignore it (i.e. add no labels to PVs, but admit it; now the admission is denied on error)

Or `GetAzureDiskLabels` [deep inside the cloud provider](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/d9d45306df052aa5824fd8b2dab4e61f5ecc481c/staging/src/k8s.io/legacy-cloud-providers/azure/azure_managedDiskController.go#L368-L368) would see it's not initialized and return no labels, say
```
if c.Location == "" {
    // Cloud provider is not initialized.
    return nil, nil
}
```

Note that it affects 1.29 and older that still have the cloud provider. I am fixing 1.30 differently in https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/124505

@Huang-Wei do you mean that you would like to see a smaller version of #119779 for cherry-pick? Note that it is only about 10 lines of actual change. The rest is comments and tests.

Since this is already released code, I would suggest cherry-picking as-is.

Also, worth testing E2E whether the issue reproduces in v1.30.

@dsgnr do you think you can give it a try?

> @Huang-Wei do you mean that you would like to see a smaller version of #119779 for cherry-pick? Note that it is only about 10 lines of actual change. The rest is comments and tests.

yup, i'm in favor of picking the _minimum_ fix, along with a minimum test #124539:

```go
		for _, n := range allNodes {
			if !preRes.NodeNames.Has(n.Node().Name) {
				// We consider Nodes that are filtered out by PreFilterResult as rejected via UnschedulableAndUnresolvable.
				// We have to record them in NodeToStatusMap so that they won't be considered as candidates in the preemption.
				diagnosis.NodeToStatusMap[n.Node().Name] = framework.NewStatus(framework.UnschedulableAndUnresolvable, "node is filtered out by the prefilter result")
				continue
			}
			nodes = append(nodes, n)
```

b/c in addition to the "fix" part, #119779 actually introduced a slight behavior change. @sanposhiho do you think the above ^^ minimum fix + #124539 makes sense?

I think the correct behavior is to set the `null` struct to the default value when `create` or `patch`, because `json.Unmarshal` in the standard library does this as well, and I think we expect the result to be as similar as possible to `json.Unmarshal`.
```
	str := "{\"hard\":{\"limits.cpu\":null}}"
	spec := &v1.ResourceQuotaSpec{}
	json.Unmarshal([]byte(str), spec)
	// output: &ResourceQuotaSpec{Hard:ResourceList{limits.cpu: {{0 0} {<nil>}  },},Scopes:[],ScopeSelector:nil,}
```



> I would expect `kubectl` to be idempotent, and for its behaviour to result in the same end configuration regardless of the initial configuration.

So our real issue here is that we didn't set the `ResourceList` to its default value when patch.
